FILE ORGANISATION

Presentation Layer – Handles user interaction, menus, and application execution.
Service Layer – Contains the main business logic for catalog, members, loans, reports, and fine calculation.
Domain Layer – Defines the core entities, interfaces, enums, and relationships of the library system.
Persistence Layer – Handles CSV-based storage and initial data generation.
Utility Components – Provide validation, configuration, logging, ID generation, and reflection-based inspection.
Test Files – Verify the functionality of the major services, validation, and persistence components.
Data Files – Store library items, members, and loan records using CSV format.
